  "salt": "FhzQWKgdJ3v2l4hQBBW2vg==",
  "text": "Ferdiad is an Irish hero who fought his foster brother in a famous single combat. He studied on the Isle of Skye under the warrior woman Scathach, together with Cuchulainn. A curse from the goddess Macha struck the men of Ulster and left only Cuchulainn in the field. The armies of Queen Medb pressed to the border of Ulster, and Cuchulainn beat one champion after another. Medb saw Ferdiad as her last best hope, for no blade could cut his horn-hard skin. He refused the task, for a duel with his foster brother must end in death. At last Medb offered him her daughter, and he gave way and met the hero at a ford. For three days neither man could win. On the last day Cuchulainn slew him with his barbed spear. The ford took the hero's name and is now the town of Ardee.",
  "okr": {
    "objective": "Ferdiad is the hero whose long duel with his foster brother ends in grief.",
    "key_results": [
      "He trained beside Cuchulainn on the Isle of Skye.",
      "The curse of Macha left the field to him and the hero alone.",
